     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none;font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;display:inline!important;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87)\">I received the following warning when using the transfer data function\r\n for  Xenium to Visium transfer, but was able to properly use vrSpatialFeaturePlot. What does this mean?</span>\r\n<div style=\"text-decoration:none;font-family:Roboto,RobotoDraft,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;color:rgba(0,0,0,0.87)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-family:Consolas,&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace,monospace;font-size:13.8667px;outline:currentcolor;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;line-height:1.1;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"outline:currentcolor\"><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">In\r\n vrCoordinates.vrAssay(from_object, reg = TRUE) : There are no registered spatial systems with name main!</span></span></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Also I&#39;m noticing that not all the visium spots are visible in the visum_pseudo plot image, and seems to be only covering a portion of the image.  Shouldn&#39;t an equal number of spots be represented between visium and visium_pseudo?<span></span></div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p style=\"text-decoration:none;font-size:11pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;margin:0px;line-height:1.5;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:black\">Vineeth Raghuram<span> </span></span></b><span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:black\">,<span> </span><b>Ph.D</b>.</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt\"></span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-decoration:none;font-size:11pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;margin:0px;line-height:1.5;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10pt;color:black;background-color:white\">Senior Scientist I</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-decoration:none;font-size:11pt;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;margin:0px;line-